  "title": "Etiquettes to be observed during Journey to Imam Husayn's (a) tomb and inside his Holy Shrine",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "The etiquettes that must be observed by those who intend to undertake pilgrimage to Imam al-Husayn’s holy shrine are clarified in the following points:\n\nFirst: As is instructed by Imam al-Sadiq (‘a), one who intends to visit the tomb of Imam al-Husayn (‘a) must first of all observe fasting for three consecutive days before he/she leaves his/her home and then bathe himself/herself on the third day.\n\nIn the introductory acts of ziyarah on the ‘Id Days, Shaykh Muhammad ibn al-Mashhadi has mentioned that if you intend to visit the holy tomb of Imam al-Husayn (‘a), you may observe fasting for three days, bathe yourself on the third day, gather your family members and dependants, and then say the following supplicatory prayer:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَسْتَوْدِعُكَ الْيَوْمَ نَفْسِيْ وَ اَهْلِيْ وَ مَالِيْ وَ وُلْدِيْ وَ كُلَّ مَنْ كَانَ مِنِّيْ بِسَبِيْلٍ الشَّاهِدَ مِنْهُمْ وَ الْغَاۤئِبَ اَللّٰهُمَّ احْفَظْنَا [بِحِفْظِكَ‏] بِحِفْظِ الْاِيمَانِ وَ احْفَظْ عَلَيْنَا اَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْنَا فِيْ حِرْزِكَ وَ لَا تَسْلُبْنَا نِعْمَتَكَ وَ لَا تُغَيِّرْ مَا بِنَا مِنْ نِعْمَةٍ وَ عَافِيَةٍ وَ زِدْنَا مِنْ فَضْلِكَ اِنَّاۤ اِلَيْكَ رَاغِبُوْنَ.\nAALLAAHUMA AINIY AASTAWDIA'UKA ALYAWMA NAFSIY WA AAHLIY WA MAALIY WA WULDIY WA KULA MAN KAANA MINIY BISABIYLIN ALSHAAHIDA MINHUM WA ALGHAA'IBA AALLAAHUMA AHFAZNAA [BIHIFZIKA] BIHIFZI ALAIYMAANI WA AHFAZ A'ALAYNAA AALLAAHUMA AJA'ALNAA FIY HIRZIKA WA LAA TASLUBNAA NIA'MATAKA WA LAA TUGHAYIR MAA BINAA MIN NIA'MAHIN WA A'AAFIYAHIN WA ZIDNAA MIN FADLIKA AINAA AILAYKA RAAGHIBUWNA.\nThe etiquettes that must be observed by those who intend to undertake pilgrimage to Imam alHusayn’s holy shrine are clarified in the following points:\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللهُ وَ اللهُ اَكْبَرُ وَ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ\nLAA AILAAHA AILAA U WA U AAKBARU WA ALHAMDU LILAAHI\nFirst: As is instructed by Imam alSadiq (‘a), one who intends to visit the tomb of Imam alHusayn (‘a) must first of all observe fasting for three consecutive days before he/she leaves his/her home and then bathe himself/herself on the third day.\nاَللهُ اَكْبَرُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللهُ\nAALLHU AAKBARU LAA AILAAHA AILAA U\nIn the introductory acts of ziyarah on the ‘Id Days, Shaykh Muhammad ibn alMashhadi has mentioned that if you intend to visit the holy tomb of Imam alHusayn (‘a), you may observe fasting for three days, bathe yourself on the third day, gather your family members and dependants, and then say the following supplicatory prayer:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ اٰدَمَ صَفْوَةِ اللّٰهِ اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ نُوْحٍ نَبِيِّ اللّٰهِ اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ خَلِيْلِ اللّٰهِ اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ مُوْسٰى كَلِيْمِ اللّٰهِ اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ عِيسٰى رُوْحِ اللّٰهِ اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ مُحَمَّدٍ حَبِيْبِ اللّٰهِ اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ عَلِيٍّ وَصِيِّ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ الْحَسَنِ الرَّضِيِّ اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ فَاطِمَةَ بِنْتِ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الشَّهِيْدُ الصِّدِّيْقُ اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْوَصِيُّ الْبَآرُّ التَّقِيُّ اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْاَرْوَاحِ الَّتِيْ حَلَّتْ بِفِنَاۤئِكَ وَ اَنَاخَتْ بِرَحْلِكَ اَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مَلَاۤئِكَةِ اللّٰهِ الْمُحْدِقِيْنَ بِكَ اَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ قَدْ اَقَمْتَ الصَّلَاةَ وَ اٰتَيْتَ الزَّكَاةَ وَ اَمَرْتَ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَ نَهَيْتَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَ عَبَدْتَ اللّٰهَ مُخْلِصًا حَتّٰى اَتَاكَ الْيَقِيْنُ اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ وَ رَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَ بَرَكَاتُهٗ.\nAALSALAAMU A'ALAYKA YAA WAARITHA AAADAMA SAFWAHI I AALSALAAMU A'ALAYKA YAA WAARITHA NUWHIN NABIYI I AALSALAAMU A'ALAYKA YAA WAARITHA AIBRAAHIYMA KHALIYLI I AALSALAAMU A'ALAYKA YAA WAARITHA MUWSAAAA KALIYMI I AALSALAAMU A'ALAYKA YAA WAARITHA A'IYSAAAA RUWHI I AALSALAAMU A'ALAYKA YAA WAARITHA MUHAMADIN HABIYBI I AALSALAAMU A'ALAYKA YAA WAARITHA A'ALIYIN WASIYI RASUWLI I AALSALAAMU A'ALAYKA YAA WAARITHA ALHASANI ALRADIYI AALSALAAMU A'ALAYKA YAA WAARITHA FAATIMAHA BINTI RASUWLI I AALSALAAMU A'ALAYKA AAYUHAA ALSHAHIYDU ALSIDIYQU AALSALAAMU A'ALAYKA AAYUHAA ALWASIYU ALBAAAARU ALTAQIYU AALSALAAMU A'ALAAA ALAARWAAHI ALATIY HALAT BIFINAA'IKA WA AANAAKHAT BIRAHLIKA AALSALAAMU A'ALAAAA MALAA'IKAHI I ALMUHDIQIYNA BIKA AASHHADU AANAKA QAD AAQAMTA ALSALAAHA WA AAATAYTA ALZAKAAHA WA AAMARTA BIALMAA'RUWFI WA NAHAYTA A'ANI ALMUNKARI WA A'ABADTA A MUKHLISANA HATAAAA AATAAKA ALYAQIYNU AALSALAAMU A'ALAYKA WA RAHMAHU I WA BARAKAATUHU.\nO Allah, I beseech You on this day to accept as trusts with You my self, my family members, my property, my children, whatever belongs to me, and whatever for which I am responsible, the present and the absent. O Allah, (please do) protect us with the protection of faith and safeguard us. O Allah, (please do) make us under Your shelter, do not deprive us of Your bounty, do not change the bliss and good health that we are enjoying, and provide us with more favor of You. Indeed, we desire for You.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا حُجَّةَ اللّٰهِ فِيۤ اَرْضِهٖ وَ سَمَاۤئِهٖ.\nAALSALAAMU A'ALAYKA YAA HUJAHA I FIY AARDIHI WA SAMAA'IHI.\nYou may then leave your house while you are in a state of submission. You may repeat as many times as possible the following statements:\nسُبْحَانَ الَّذِيْ لَا تَنْفَدُ خَزَاۤئِنُهٗ سُبْحَانَ الَّذِيْ لَا تَبِيْدُ مَعَالِمُهٗ سُبْحَانَ الَّذِيْ لَا يَفْنٰى مَا عِنْدَهٗ سُبْحَانَ الَّذِيْ لَا يُشْرِكُ اَحَدًا فِيْ حُكْمِهٖ سُبْحَانَ الَّذِيْ لَا اضْمِحْلَالَ لِفَخْرِهٖ سُبْحَانَ الَّذِيْ لَا انْقِطَاعَ لِمُدَّتِهٖ سُبْحَانَ الَّذِيْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ غَيْرُهٗ.\nSUBHAANA ALADHIY LAA TANFADU KHAZAA'INUHU SUBHAANA ALADHIY LAA TABIYDU MAA'AALIMUHU SUBHAANA ALADHIY LAA YAFNAAAA MAA A'INDAHU SUBHAANA ALADHIY LAA YUSHRIKU AAHADANA FIY HUKMIHI SUBHAANA ALADHIY LAA ADMIHLAALA LIFAKHRIHI SUBHAANA ALADHIY LAA ANQITAAA'A LIMUDATIHI SUBHAANA ALADHIY LAA AILAAHA GHAYRUHU.\nThere is no god save Allah. Allah is the Most Great. All praise be to Allah.\nسُبْحَانَ ذِي الْجَلَالِ الْبَاذِخِ الْعَظِيْمِ سُبْحَانَ ذِي الْعِزِّ الشَّامِخِ الْمُنِيْفِ سُبْحَانَ ذِي الْمُلْكِ الْفَاخِرِ الْقَدِيْمِ سُبْحَانَ ذِي الْبَهْجَةِ وَ الْجَمَالِ سُبْحَانَ مَنْ تَرَدَّى بِالنُّوْرِ وَ الْوَقَارِ سُبْحَانَ مَنْ يَرٰى اَثَرَ النَّمْلِ فِيْ الصَّفَا وَ وَقْعَ الطَّيْرِ فِي الْهَوَاۤءِ.\nSUBHAANA DHIY ALJALAALI ALBAADHIKHI ALA'AZIYMI SUBHAANA DHIY ALA'IZI ALSHAAMIKHI ALMUNIYFI SUBHAANA DHIY ALMULKI ALFAAKHIRI ALQADIYMI SUBHAANA DHIY ALBAHJAHI WA ALJAMAALI SUBHAANA MAN TARADAAA BIALNUWRI WA ALWAQAARI SUBHAANA MAN YARAAAA AATHARA ALNAMLI FIY ALSAFAA WA WAQA'A ALTAYRI FIY ALHAWAA'I.\nYou may also repeat statements of glorification of Almighty Allah and invocations of His blessings upon the Holy Prophet and his Household. You may also walk with gravity and tranquility."
